Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: bound the AP Capability Report's AP Radio Basic Capabilities walk

0261 bounded handle_ap_radio_basic_cap() on the WSC M1 path (em_configuration.cpp). The AP
Capability Report carries the same TLV, and em_capability_t::handle_ap_radio_basic_cap() walks it
with the same code: op class entries by their own channel counts, unchecked against the TLV's length
or the 64-channel list it copies them into. A malformed entry (an agent's op class 1 with 129
channels, the hole 0260 removes on the agent) would overrun op_class_info on the stack here as it did
on the M1 path, from any device answering an AP Capability Query. The same three bounds as 0261: the
TLV must hold its fixed part, an entry must lie within the TLV with at most EM_MAX_CHANNELS_IN_LIST
channels, and a new op class must fit the data model's list (EM_MAX_OPCLASS); the rest of a
malformed TLV is ignored, logged.

Platform-independent.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp b/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
index 4e1c807..ad64ff3 100644
--- a/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
+++ b/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
@@ -1188,6 +1188,10 @@ int em_capability_t::handle_ap_radio_basic_cap(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int
 
 	dm_easy_mesh_t *dm = get_data_model();
 
+	if (len < sizeof(em_ap_radio_basic_cap_t)) {
+		em_printfout("AP Radio Basic Capabilities TLV too short: %u bytes", len);
+		return -1;
+	}
 	memcpy(ruid, radio_basic_cap->ruid, sizeof(mac_address_t));
 	dm_easy_mesh_t::macbytes_to_string(ruid, mac_str);
 	for (i = 0; i < dm->get_num_radios(); i++) {
@@ -1217,6 +1221,16 @@ int em_capability_t::handle_ap_radio_basic_cap(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int
 	basic_cap_op_class = radio_basic_cap->op_classes;
 	if (basic_cap_op_class != NULL) {
 		for (i = 0; i < radio_basic_cap->op_class_num; i++) {
+			// an entry and its channels lie within the TLV, and the channels fit the list, as 0261 makes the WSC M1's walk
+			// (em_configuration.cpp): the AP Capability Report carries the same TLV and its walk would overrun op_class_info alike
+			unsigned char *entry = reinterpret_cast<unsigned char *> (basic_cap_op_class);
+			if ((entry + sizeof(em_op_class_t) > buff + len) ||
+			    (entry + sizeof(em_op_class_t) + basic_cap_op_class->num > buff + len) ||
+			    (basic_cap_op_class->num > EM_MAX_CHANNELS_IN_LIST)) {
+				em_printfout("Radio %s: op class entry %u of %u malformed (TLV %u bytes): ignoring the rest",
+					mac_str, i, radio_basic_cap->op_class_num, len);
+				break;
+			}
 			memset(&op_class_info, 0, sizeof(em_op_class_info_t));
 			memcpy(op_class_info.id.ruid, ruid, sizeof(mac_address_t));
 			op_class_info.id.type = em_op_class_type_capability;
@@ -1242,6 +1256,10 @@ int em_capability_t::handle_ap_radio_basic_cap(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int
 			if (op_class_exists == true) {
 				op_class_exists = false;
 			} else {
+				if (dm->get_num_op_class() >= EM_MAX_OPCLASS) {
+					em_printfout("Radio %s: op class list full (%u): ignoring the rest", mac_str, dm->get_num_op_class());
+					break;
+				}
 				op_class_obj = &dm->m_op_class[dm->get_num_op_class()];
 				dm->set_num_op_class(dm->get_num_op_class() + 1);
 			}
